  "corpus": {
    "statement": "EIGHT DOCUMENTS IS THE CORPUS, and it stays eight until production traffic adds to it. This is an enumeration, not an estimate: on 2026-09-30 all six sandbox MinIO buckets were listed in full (4061 objects), every PDF under every sustainment prefix was fetched and hashed, and the result was 8 distinct document contents -- every one of which is already a TARGETS row, and every TARGETS row of which has a PDF. There is no unseen notice sitting in the bucket. The corpus therefore does not widen by looking harder; it widens when new notices are ingested. Enumerated in docs/pcn-corpus-widening-2026-09-30.md, which also lists the extensions present and absent corpus-wide.",
    "why_it_is_here": "This block exists so the denominator lives where the GATE READS IT rather than only in prose. pcn_corpus_run.check_ground_truth() asserts TARGETS against it at startup and aborts on a disagreement, and pcn_corpus_gate.py copies it into docs/corpus-gate/latest.json so a committed report states the corpus it was measured against. A denominator that only a human can check is a denominator that drifts.",
